  "notes": [
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes.emphasis",
      "message": "emphasis defaults by intent: low when informational, high when promotional (Tag.tsx L81). Both values carry their emphasis prop, so a promotional Tag at Low emphasis emits emphasis=\"low\" and one at High emphasis is unambiguous whatever the intent. Intent picks the padding, radius and font (tags.ts L9-L22); emphasis and colorScheme pick the colours (tagEmphasisColorMap[emphasis][colorScheme], Tag.tsx L107)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "axes",
      "message": "Tag renders a Box, not Interactable or Pressable (Tag.tsx L117-L132), and Tag.css styles only nodeCss (L25-L28), so the Contract has no State axis."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "paint",
      "message": "Tag paints its colours inline as rgb(theme.spectrum[<key>]) (Tag.tsx L107-L114) over Box's background=\"bg\" (Tag.tsx L120), the key from tagEmphasisColorMap (tags.ts L32-L85). The Foundations document carries each as tag-<emphasis>-<colorScheme>-<background|color>, aliasing the scheme's Primitive in each Mode."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "layout.Label.textStyle",
      "message": "A promotional Tag sets its label in caption (tagFontMap, tags.ts L14-L17), which CDS draws uppercase (--text-textTransform: var(--textTransform-caption)). A Text Style has no text case, so the Figma label keeps the case it is typed in."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "family",
      "message": "background and color (@danger custom spectrum colours, Tag.tsx L52-L55) override the colour scheme, and maxWidth (L56-L57) truncates the label (overflow=\"truncate\", L149); without one nothing truncates. The Box layout props (paddingX, paddingY, gap, font and the rest, L91-L102) override the defaults the Contract draws. None of them is an axis."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "properties.startIcon",
      "message": "startIconActive and endIconActive (Tag.tsx L62-L69) pick the active glyph of the same icon; the icon source uses the inactive glyphs only. start and end (L58-L65) take any React node, and win over startIcon and endIcon (L133-L139, L156-L162); the Contract models the icon names, at Icon size xs (L137, L160)."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "code",
      "message": "CDS's own Code Connect file (Tag.figma.ts) maps intent, emphasis and colorScheme as the Contract does (L8-L25), and always emits emphasis (L33). It maps no icons; the Contract adds startIcon and endIcon from Tag.tsx."
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "at": "paint",
      "message": "The deprecated tagColorMap (tags.ts L95-L102) is the old name of tagEmphasisColorMap by intent; Tag.tsx reads tagEmphasisColorMap (L107)."
    }
  ],
